WEBVTT

00:00:19.048 --> 00:00:22.925
This is Milestone 3 as reconciled against your
architecture, recorded on the live staging

00:00:22.985 --> 00:00:26.862
Portal. It begins with the Registers.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.890
Your v1.0 Registers are loaded: sixty seven
Fields, all twenty nine distinguishing lines,

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.890
four hundred and nineteen Specialties and the
alias set, yours to maintain without a

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.890
developer.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:46.060
Here are the crowded neighbours. Public
Health, Health Policy, Public Policy, Public

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.560
Administration. The line beside each is the
one that helps somebody choose.

00:00:51.172 --> 00:00:55.421
Renaming a term here changes every profile
that uses it at once. Retiring one stops

00:00:55.481 --> 00:00:59.730
offering it, and leaves it exactly where it
already is.

00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:12.880
A direct invitation, as in Milestone 2. Name
only, link copied, sent by hand.

00:01:20.075 --> 00:01:23.022
Ingrid has registered, and this is what is
new. Her profile and the community are one

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:26.029
click away.

00:01:27.473 --> 00:01:31.913
The first time she opens her profile, the
Collaborator Profile Standards appear. No

00:01:31.973 --> 00:01:36.413
checkbox. The Portal records that she was
shown them, with the version, date and time.

00:01:37.034 --> 00:01:40.198
She will not see them interrupt again. They
stay readable from Profile Standards at the

00:01:40.258 --> 00:01:43.422
top of the page.

00:01:43.492 --> 00:01:46.811
Each part of the profile saves on its own,
because people do this over several sittings

00:01:46.871 --> 00:01:50.190
and often on a phone.

00:01:50.251 --> 00:01:54.691
She is not yet in the directory. Readiness is
your six items: name, Professional Identity,

00:01:54.751 --> 00:01:59.191
About Your Work, a Field, country and a
photograph. Nothing optional counts.

00:02:02.832 --> 00:02:05.772
The photograph, with your guidance: an
individual professional image, no logos or

00:02:05.832 --> 00:02:08.772
group photographs, and cultural and religious
dress welcome. It is part of readiness, and

00:02:08.832 --> 00:02:11.772
cropped to one portrait rectangle.

00:02:15.096 --> 00:02:19.438
Professional Identity, with your prompt. In
her own words, and not a place for

00:02:19.498 --> 00:02:23.840
credentials, Fields or achievements, which
each have their own.

00:02:27.159 --> 00:02:31.599
About Your Work. Your prompt, word for word:
written for collaborators outside her own

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:36.099
field. Up to five hundred characters, and
required for readiness.

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:43.225
About is the optional longer section, up to
two thousand characters, for broader context.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:48.308
Country is shown to collaborators. City stays
with the Institute. That was the promise made

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:52.586
when it was asked for, and the screen says so.

00:02:55.544 --> 00:02:59.984
Up to three current positions, now with
country and start year. Only the title is

00:03:00.044 --> 00:03:04.484
required, so a role that sits inside no
organisation needs none.

00:03:10.581 --> 00:03:14.303
Where her work belongs. The orientation opens
by itself the first time, now in your own

00:03:14.363 --> 00:03:18.085
words, and never interrupts again.

00:03:18.161 --> 00:03:22.601
A Field describes the discipline she brings to
questions of longer lives. It does not require

00:03:22.661 --> 00:03:27.101
longer lives to be the discipline itself.
Classify lightly. Describe richly.

00:03:29.471 --> 00:03:33.069
Type Longevity and the Portal explains, as
your Field Register asks, rather than listing

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:36.727
everything longevity related.

00:03:39.066 --> 00:03:44.028
Search first, never a list to scroll. Sixty
seven Fields are nothing to a search.

00:03:46.498 --> 00:03:49.414
Type the word you use. Physiotherapy leads to
Physical Therapy, and the screen quietly says

00:03:49.474 --> 00:03:52.390
why.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:00.196
A Specialty is optional. Selecting one never
assigns her a Field. A journalist who writes

00:04:00.256 --> 00:04:04.102
about health policy is a journalist.

00:04:04.983 --> 00:04:08.240
And no dead end. If nothing fits, she writes
the term she uses and carries on. The

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.557
Institute decides later.

00:04:16.946 --> 00:04:20.606
With a Field chosen, all six are present. Your
profile is ready for Directory Review, with

00:04:20.666 --> 00:04:24.326
Preview my profile beside it.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.846
Credentials after the name, up to three,
chosen from the library rather than typed.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.640
The same letters, several records. FRCP
differs between London, Edinburgh and Glasgow,

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:41.140
and the meaning beside each is how she picks
the one she holds.

00:04:44.371 --> 00:04:48.062
And the meaning is searchable as well as the
letters. Somebody who does not think of

00:04:48.122 --> 00:04:51.813
themselves as an MPH still finds it.

00:05:00.461 --> 00:05:03.401
Preview, as another collaborator sees it.
Credentials after the name, her Professional

00:05:03.461 --> 00:05:06.401
Identity, About Your Work beneath it,
positions with country and year. City nowhere

00:05:06.461 --> 00:05:09.401
on the page.

00:05:10.763 --> 00:05:15.203
Links show their label and never their
address. Empty sections do not appear at all,

00:05:15.263 --> 00:05:19.703
so a profile with a few things filled in reads
as deliberate.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:25.820
The directory card, restrained as you asked:
photograph, name with credentials,

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:30.320
Professional Identity and country. Nothing
else competes with the person.

00:05:31.782 --> 00:05:36.124
And from the footer of every page, somewhere
to say what she found. Your Alpha group are

00:05:36.184 --> 00:05:40.526
the most valuable readers this Portal will
ever have.

00:05:56.229 --> 00:05:59.169
Ingrid proposed Longevity Finance as a Field.
It arrives here with anything close that the

00:05:59.229 --> 00:06:02.169
vocabulary already holds, so mapping is one
click and a duplicate is hard to approve by

00:06:02.229 --> 00:06:05.169
accident.

00:06:05.697 --> 00:06:10.137
You may correct the wording before approving.
Because people select entries rather than

00:06:10.197 --> 00:06:14.637
typing text, your wording is what every
profile then shows, including hers.

00:06:16.222 --> 00:06:20.662
Approved. It is now in the vocabulary, on her
profile, and she has been told. Had you

00:06:20.722 --> 00:06:25.162
declined, nothing would have been sent:
whether to explain is yours.

00:06:30.252 --> 00:06:33.199
What the community has said about the Portal,
with the page each person was on when they

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:36.206
said it.

00:07:00.517 --> 00:07:03.836
Tomas, a geriatrician, searches for an actuary
and finds Ingrid. Two people who would not

00:07:03.896 --> 00:07:07.215
otherwise have met.

00:07:09.533 --> 00:07:12.473
What the first Beta uses instead of messaging.
He registers an interest, the Institute sees

00:07:12.533 --> 00:07:15.473
it and passes it on. A record and a note, not
a conversation, and only because Ingrid said

00:07:15.533 --> 00:07:18.473
she was open to approaches.

00:07:30.875 --> 00:07:35.186
And here it is on your side. One collaborator
would like to work with another. Passing it on

00:07:35.246 --> 00:07:39.557
is yours to do, which at Alpha is exactly
right.
